  "note": "The standalone demo rack (issue #63) shows the meter range, and the asset source only has the meters: the E820 feeding its breakers, and seven meters connected to nothing. The rack is wired as a demonstration rack is: its incomer (~DEMO-RACK-SUPPLY, electrical.json) comes in through the GPQM144 Pro power quality meter onto the rack busbar, and every other meter feeds a load bank from it (~DEMO-LOAD-*, assumed ratings, 72.5 kW in all against the 100 kVA incomer). The load behind the E820 branch circuit monitor is split over its 126 circuits. The load banks step through a demonstration duty cycle; the meters measure it.",
